A public accessor for a face's whole metrics (GPUI patch for docs/plans/20261014-gpui-frontend.md Task 15):
`TextSystem::font_metrics` returns the `FontMetrics` the platform text system read, in font units, so a caller gets
the line gap and the underline's position and thickness, which `TextSystem` measured but never exposed (it had
`ascent`, `descent`, `cap_height`, `x_height` only). ngterm's terminal sizes its cells and its box-drawing lines from
them, as Ghostty does. An upstream candidate (Zed): read-only, no behavior change. scripts/vendor-gpui.sh applies
this after 0001.

diff -ruN a/src/text_system.rs b/src/text_system.rs
--- a/src/text_system.rs
+++ b/src/text_system.rs
@@ -514,6 +514,13 @@
         self.read_metrics(font_id, |metrics| metrics.descent(font_size))
     }
 
+    /// Get every metric of the given font as the font declares it, in font units (`FontMetrics`' methods scale
+    /// them to a font size), including those no other accessor reports: the line gap and the underline's
+    /// position and thickness.
+    pub fn font_metrics(&self, font_id: FontId) -> FontMetrics {
+        self.read_metrics(font_id, |metrics| *metrics)
+    }
+
